From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:47:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] platform: the title heap grows in 2 MiB segments

Direct memory is committed whole when it is mapped, where libc's heap takes a page
as it is touched. With 16 MiB segments and up to eight arenas, a payload sharing the
application's pool held far more than it used: a Wine helper running a game's Vulkan
driver kept 88 MiB of 16 MiB segments mapped (PS5 Pro, firmware 10.01), and the
console's peak memory rose by about 85 MiB against the same game on libc's heap.

DEFAULT_GRANULARITY goes from 16 MiB to 2 MiB, so an arena maps 2 MiB at a time, and
the segment table from 1024 to 8192 entries, enough 2 MiB segments for the whole
16 GiB range, so a title's large heap is not cut short by the table. Blocks past the
32 MiB mapping threshold keep their own segment as before.

A new host check: an arena's first segment is its 2 MiB granularity. make test: 321 of
321 checks; make builds the console library with -Werror. Not yet measured on the console.

Backported to b83202be for PS5LM Lean from mihawk-99/PS5_PayloadSDK commit 9d0487845ad50e3a266872cbbaaedc6ffafe3404. Whole commit.
---
 platform/src/dlmalloc/mspace.c | 10 +++++++---
 platform/src/heap.c            |  4 +++-
 platform/tests/test_platform.c |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/src/dlmalloc/mspace.c b/platform/src/dlmalloc/mspace.c
index 5692d26..2324501 100644
--- a/platform/src/dlmalloc/mspace.c
+++ b/platform/src/dlmalloc/mspace.c
@@ -33,9 +33,13 @@ int ps5p_heap_unmap(void *address, size_t bytes);
  * are 32: its compilers emit 32-byte-aligned AVX stores into plain new
  * objects. */
 #define MALLOC_ALIGNMENT ((size_t)32)
-/* Each arena maps this much at a time: small enough that arenas a title
- * barely uses hold little direct memory. */
-#define DEFAULT_GRANULARITY ((size_t)16 << 20)
+/* Each arena maps this much at a time. Direct memory is committed whole when it
+ * is mapped, unlike libc's heap, whose pages are taken as they are touched: a
+ * payload that shares the application's pool (a Wine helper's Vulkan driver,
+ * eight arenas) held 88 MiB of 16 MiB segments where libc's heap had held about
+ * a tenth of it. 2 MiB keeps an idle arena's share small; src/heap.c's segment
+ * table is sized for the larger count of segments this makes. */
+#define DEFAULT_GRANULARITY ((size_t)2 << 20)
 #define DEFAULT_MMAP_THRESHOLD ((size_t)32 << 20)
 #define MALLOC_FAILURE_ACTION errno = ENOMEM
 #define NO_MALLINFO 1
diff --git a/platform/src/heap.c b/platform/src/heap.c
index 3a95d30..262c57a 100644
--- a/platform/src/heap.c
+++ b/platform/src/heap.c
@@ -44,7 +44,9 @@ size_t mspace_usable_size(const void *pointer);
 void mspace_free(mspace space, void *pointer);
 
 
-#define HEAP_MAX_SEGMENTS 1024
+/* Enough segments of the arenas' 2 MiB granularity (src/dlmalloc/mspace.c) to
+ * fill the whole range: 16 GiB / 2 MiB. */
+#define HEAP_MAX_SEGMENTS 8192
 #define HEAP_UNIT PS5P_DIRECT_UNIT
 #define HEAP_PROTECTION (PS5_KERNEL_PROT_CPU_READ | PS5_KERNEL_PROT_CPU_WRITE)
 
diff --git a/platform/tests/test_platform.c b/platform/tests/test_platform.c
index aa1a588..94728f2 100644
--- a/platform/tests/test_platform.c
+++ b/platform/tests/test_platform.c
@@ -1055,6 +1055,8 @@ test_heap(void)
    check((uintptr_t)small % 32 == 0, "heap: blocks are 32-byte aligned");
    check(stats.segments == 1 && host_direct_allocations() == direct_before + 1,
          "heap: the first block maps one segment");
+   check(stats.mapped_bytes <= ((size_t)2 << 20),
+         "heap: an arena's first segment is its 2 MiB granularity, not more");
    strcpy(small, "title heap");
    char *grown = __wrap_realloc(small, 100000);
    check(grown && ps5_heap_owns(grown) && strcmp(grown, "title heap") == 0,
